    {
      "id": "duo-coordination",
      "type": "overview",
      "title": "Duo Coordination",
      "toc": true,
      "visible": true,
      "order": 3,
      "paragraphs": [
        "Both bosses are alive at once. Wulfric is the melee-pressure threat; Elswyth is the spell and ground-control threat. Their danger is the overlap — Elswyth's chaos-flame on the ground while Wulfric forces you into melee range.",
        "Neither boss is a 'passive' partner. Treat the fight as managing two concurrent threat patterns, then pick a kill order that fits your build."
      ],
      "bullets": [
        "Wulfric: melee pressure, sword/fire/blood.",
        "Elswyth: spell + ground control, chaos-flame/rune/teleport.",
        "Danger is the overlap of both at once."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "boss-a-profile",
      "type": "overview",
      "title": "Wulfric Profile",
      "toc": true,
      "visible": true,
      "order": 4,
      "paragraphs": [
        "Thane Wulfric is the melee-pressure boss. He uses sword combos, fire projectiles and Blood Spike. He wants to stay on top of you, so kiting him is harder than kiting Elswyth.",
        "His pressure is constant; the window to damage him is between his combos, not during."
      ],
      "bullets": [
        "Role: melee pressure.",
        "Key: sword combo, fire projectile, Blood Spike.",
        "Punish after combos."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "boss-b-profile",
      "type": "overview",
      "title": "Elswyth Profile",
      "toc": true,
      "visible": true,
      "order": 5,
      "paragraphs": [
        "Lady Elswyth is the spell and ground-control boss. Her chaos-flame, runes and teleports shape the arena. She is easier to kite but punishes standing still with ground effects.",
        "She is the source of most Chaos damage in the fight; respect her ground."
      ],
      "bullets": [
        "Role: spell / ground control.",
        "Key: chaos-flame, rune, teleport.",
        "Keep moving through her ground."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "combined-attacks",
      "type": "overview",
      "title": "Combined Attacks",
      "toc": true,
      "visible": true,
      "order": 6,
      "paragraphs": [
        "The deadliest moments are when both act together: Elswyth drops chaos-flame while Wulfric closes for a sword combo, or a Blood Spike lands inside a rune. These overlaps are why build-specific kill order matters.",
        "When you see both telegraph at once, create space — do not trade into the overlap."
      ],
      "bullets": [
        "Chaos-flame + sword combo = biggest overlap.",
        "Blood Spike inside a rune = space denial.",
        "Create distance on double telegraphs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "target-priority",
      "type": "overview",
      "title": "Target Priority (Build-Dependent)",
      "toc": true,
      "visible": true,
      "order": 7,
      "paragraphs": [
        "There is no single correct kill order. The logic: if your build hates sustained ground control, kill Elswyth first to remove chaos-flame; if your build cannot survive melee chase, kill Wulfric first to remove the pressure.",
        "The facts do not change between builds — only your suggested priority and reason change. Verify on the current patch which order feels safer for your skill set."
      ],
      "bullets": [
        "Hate ground control -> Elswyth first.",
        "Hate melee chase -> Wulfric first.",
        "Facts are constant; priority is build-specific."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "arena-and-separation",
      "type": "arena",
      "title": "Arena and Separation",
      "toc": true,
      "visible": true,
      "order": 8,
      "paragraphs": [
        "The Holten Estate arena allows separation: you can often pull one boss toward a corner or edge to fight them more narrowly. This is a legitimate tactic on the current patch when it works.",
        "After one dies, the other's behavior may shift — confirm on the current patch whether the survivor enrages or changes pattern."
      ],
      "bullets": [
        "Separation is a real tactic, not an exploit.",
        "Pull one boss to a corner to narrow the fight.",
        "Check survivor behavior after a kill."
      ]
    },
